# The slow tests (17.3): tests that take most of the 200 s limit or more through
# dcfs, kept out of the normal set so that a shard fits its job, and run with a
# limit of 1500 s by the weekly set (xfstests_slow_<n>.sh; lists
# xfstests.slow.<fstype>.*). Their native times are in the reasons. Whether the
# slowness is dcfs's or the host's load is plan step 17.3's to find out (the
# results line of each test carries the daemon's CPU time for it). This file is
# the global set; xfstests.<fstype>.slow has the tests slow on one backing only.
